{"ts": 0.062605, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;38;5;208mOrientation\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nIn a moment you'll be at the practice prompt below. It looks like:\r\n\r\n    \u001b[2mshelltutor>\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nType a command, press Enter — the shell runs it. The terminal is\r\nkeyboard-only; you can't click mid-line to move the cursor. Resize\r\nyour terminal larger if text wraps (80×24 or bigger).\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5;244mFour words steer the tutor:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mnext\u001b[0m  advance        \u001b[1;38;5;220mprev\u001b[0m  go back\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mshow\u001b[0m  redisplay      \u001b[1;38;5;220mquit\u001b[0m  leave (progress saved)\r\n\r\nA fifth word, \u001b[1;38;5;220mcheck\u001b[0m, appears at gate tasks when relevant.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5;208m▶ Type \u001b[1;38;5;220mnext\u001b[1;38;5;208m to begin Stage 1.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 684}
