{"ts": 0.098489, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;38;5;208m1.1 — running commands\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nAt the prompt below, type this and press Enter:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mecho hello\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nYou'll see \u001b[2mhello\u001b[0m printed, then the prompt comes back. Now try:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mecho I am at the shell\u001b[0m      \u001b[2m# spaces separate words\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mecho \"I am at the shell\"\u001b[0m    \u001b[2m# quotes group them into one\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5;220mecho\u001b[0m just repeats its words back. It is the simplest command\r\nthere is, and its shape is the shape of every command you'll meet:\r\na name, then the words you hand it.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5;208m▶ Try all three, then type \u001b[1;38;5;220mnext\u001b[1;38;5;208m.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 635}
