{"ts": 0.242645, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;38;5;208m1.3 — where am I, who am I, when is it\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree commands that ask the system about itself.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mwhoami\u001b[0m     \u001b[2m# the user name you're logged in as\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mpwd\u001b[0m        \u001b[2m# print working directory — the folder you're in\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mdate\u001b[0m       \u001b[2m# the current date and time\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nHere \u001b[1;38;5;220mpwd\u001b[0m shows the tutor's own folder, because that is where\r\nthis practice prompt starts. Stage 2 is all about folders.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5;208m▶ Run all three, then type \u001b[1;38;5;220mnext\u001b[1;38;5;208m.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 567}
