{"ts": 0.400138, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;38;5;208mSTAGE 2 — Paths and the filesystem\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree lessons, then a gate. The shell is always \u001b[1;38;5;244msomewhere\u001b[0m in\r\nthe filesystem; this stage teaches you to move around and to predict\r\nwhere files land.\r\n\r\nYou'll use:\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mls\u001b[0m    list what's in the current folder\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mcd\u001b[0m    change to another folder\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mpwd\u001b[0m   print where you are now\r\n\r\nAnd the path symbols:\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;244m.\u001b[0m     this folder\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;244m..\u001b[0m    the parent folder\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;244m~\u001b[0m     your home folder\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5;208m▶ Type \u001b[1;38;5;220mnext\u001b[1;38;5;208m to begin lesson 2.1.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 632}
{"ts": 0.400269, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.414587, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[2m(type \u001b[1;38;5;220mnext\u001b[0m\u001b[2m to advance — or \u001b[0m\u001b[1;38;5;220mprev\u001b[2m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;38;5;220mshow\u001b[2m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;38;5;220mquit\u001b[2m)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 140}
